---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/faq/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          Otto FAQs: Access, Setup, Support &amp; Practice Fit
        </span>
      </nav>
      <section class="tool-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Questions worth asking</div>
        <h1>Get a clearer picture of Otto.</h1>
        <p>Direct answers, with links to the details.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Who is Otto designed for?</summary>
          <p>
            Otto is designed for independent mental health practices, with an
            early focus on solo, self-pay care. If you need insurance claims,
            prescribing, supervision, or a multi-provider workflow, confirm
            current support before planning a move.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Otto offer more than AI note drafting?</summary>
          <p>
            The public product page also lists scheduling, telehealth, patient
            records, and payments. See the{" "}
            <a href="/mental-health-ehr/">mental health EHR overview</a> for the
            workflow.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which note formats does Otto describe?</summary>
          <p>
            Otto lists SOAP and DAP notes. The clinician reviews, edits, and
            signs the draft. Read about{" "}
            <a href="/ai-progress-notes/">AI progress notes</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What can I use on this site today?</summary>
          <p>
            Watch the <a href="/demo/#watch">product demo</a> and use the{" "}
            <a href="/tools/">free tools</a> and <a href="/templates/">note
            templates</a> without signing up. The signup and product tour are
            previews. They do not create an Otto account or grant product access.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does a superbill guarantee reimbursement?</summary>
          <p>
            Payment depends on the client’s plan, benefits, deductible,
            eligibility, and submission requirements. A superbill supplies
            information for a claim. Read the{" "}
            <a href="/blog/superbill-for-therapy/">superbill guide</a>.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are these free tools part of the EHR?</summary>
          <p>
            These are standalone browser tools. This resource site does not
            establish that the same workflows are integrated into the Otto EHR.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do the free tools upload or save my entries?</summary>
          <p>
            The tools calculate and build documents in the browser without
            submitting entries to a server or saving them in browser storage.
            Downloads and printouts contain the entered information. Use
            fictitious client details in this review version.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>
            Can I import existing records or use insurance claims?
          </summary>
          <p>
            Current support and limits need to be confirmed with Otto. Ask for a
            demonstration using the record formats, payers, and workflows your
            practice needs.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where can I review data handling and BAA terms?</summary>
          <p>
            Start with the <a href="/security/">security review questions</a>{" "}
            and request written, Otto-specific answers. This site does not
            verify BAA availability or recording-retention terms.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <section class="product-section" id="getting-started" aria-labelledby="getting-started-heading">
        <h2 id="getting-started-heading">Access, setup, and support.</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details>
            <summary>What does joining the waitlist mean?</summary>
            <p>
              A waitlist expresses interest in future access. Access timing,
              eligibility, pricing, and trial terms need to be confirmed before
              you plan to use Otto with clients. This site’s signup is demo-only
              and does not reserve a place.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens after I try the signup?</summary>
            <p>
              You see a preview confirmation. Nothing is submitted or saved,
              and no confirmation or follow-up email is sent. You can continue
              with the <a href="/demo/#watch">demo</a> or the free resources.
              Follow-up timing for live signup has not been announced here.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What should I confirm before my first session?</summary>
            <p>
              Ask who will help with setup, what training is available, and how
              to get help during a visit. Walk through a fictional session,
              correct a note draft, and review the payment step. Confirm current
              capabilities, data terms, and any setup fees before entering
              patient information. Onboarding services and support hours for
              Otto still need to be confirmed.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How should I plan a switch from my current EHR?</summary>
            <p>
              Use the <a href="/switch/">switching checklist</a> to identify the
              records and workflows you need to carry over. Confirm import
              formats, costs, timing, and who checks the transfer. Plan continued
              access to your existing records before choosing a cutover date.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>I’m already a customer. Where do I get help?</summary>
            <p>
              If you already use Otto, use the support contact provided with
              your account. Existing Tebra customers can find contact options in
              the <a href="https://helpme.tebra.com/Contact_Us">Tebra Help Center</a>.
              The waitlist preview does not send support requests or change an
              existing account.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>See what you would review in Otto.</h2>
            <p>
              Watch a visit move through note drafting, clinician review, and
              payment. No signup is needed to watch.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/demo/#watch">
            Watch the demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .faq-list a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
</style>
